<Testimonial
  title="Testimonial | Gino Nérèo"
  heading="Gino Nérèo"
  description="Gino travelled from the Netherlands to ordain in Belgium and offer a blessing to his mother, and found that feelings pass rather than hold you."
  detail="11th European Ordination Program participant"
  portrait={img2026072}
  portraitAlt="Portrait of Gino Nérèo"
>
  <p>
    My name is Gino. I came from the Netherlands to Belgium to be ordained as a monk, and to offer a blessing to my
    family - especially to my mother. As a son, this is a way to give back to the one who carried me and brought me into
    the world.
  </p>
  <p>
    To become a monk, the first step is to cut your hair. It frees you from the need to look a certain way or to feel
    attached to appearance. In that freedom, every monk begins to look the same.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ordination day is a big day. You leave behind the life of a lay person and step fully into the monkhood. Here you
    learn more deeply about Buddhism, directly from the monks themselves. Through meditation, I have found greater
    peace. Feelings arise and then simply pass, they flow over you instead of holding you stuck in one place.
  </p>
  <p>Watch the full video <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mA6R8_K2Kb0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">on YouTube</a></p>
</Testimonial>
